I'm a tinkerer who loves all things computer and math. I mainly mess around with [Zig](https://ziglang.org/) and C in my free time. 

My area of interests are computer architecture, computer systems, compilers, 
emulator development, frontend & JavaScript tooling, systems programming and more. 
I'm currently exploring the embedded space and would like to get deeper into firmware development.

Professionally, I mostly work with web technologies ranging from various front-end tooling like React, Vue, Vite and many more to back-end services and infrastructures-related technologies.

I'm quite obsessed with workflow optimization and ergonomics, I got into split keyboards in [2025](https://elyfheim.me/blog/split-keyboard/) and I think it's game-changing for my typing experience. 
And naturally I also prefer a keyboard-focused editor like [neovim](https://neovim.io/) (although, [helix](https://helix-editor.com/) is looking really nice these days).

## Projects
- [Warlock](https://warlock.elyfheim.me): A CHIP-8 emulator/interpreter written in C, compiled to WebAssembly.
- [Nordle](https://nordle.elyfheim.me): A Wordle clone built with React, written in TypeScript.

